    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Tests {@link TokenQueue#consumeCssIdentifier()} against the CSS-syntax escape/unescape cases from the web-platform-tests suite and the Chromium CSS parser tests. <p>Each case is an {@code (expected, input)} pair: {@code input} is a (possibly escaped) CSS identifier fed to the queue, and {@code expected} is the unescaped identifier that {@code consumeCssIdentifier()} should return.</p> <p>Non-ASCII and control characters in the data are built from their Unicode code points via {@link #unit(int)} and {@link #codePoint(int)} so the test data stays exact and easy to read (no invisible glyphs in the source).</p>"
   },
   {
